<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Proven lab</title>
<!-- A template. lab/seed/render.sh fills every marked place and writes the copy the lab serves into the lab's page volume.
     The password is filled in there and nowhere else: it is never committed and never baked into an image. -->
<style>
  /* Light and airy by default (the owner, 27 Oct); the same palette reads in dark when the reader's system is dark.
     Colours from saphan.ai (assets/site.css). No web fonts: the lab works offline. */
  :root {
    color-scheme: light dark;
    --ground:#f7f9f8; --surface:#ffffff; --rule:#e4e9e6; --edge:#d3dbd6;
    --ink:#13201a; --ink-body:#2a3830; --ink-code:#23302a; --ink-muted:#52625a; --ink-dim:#69786f;
    --accent:#2b6a46; --accent-hi:#1b5236; --accent-wash:rgba(43,106,70,0.09); --accent-edge:rgba(43,106,70,0.35);
    --bad:#a8402f; --bad-wash:rgba(168,64,47,0.09);
    --logo:#13201a;
    --sans: ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --ground:#0c0e0d; --surface:#101312; --rule:#1d211e; --edge:#22271f;
      --ink:#eef1ef; --ink-body:#d6dad7; --ink-code:#c3cbc5; --ink-muted:#9aa39d; --ink-dim:#758078;
      --accent:#86a98f; --accent-hi:#a3c2ab; --accent-wash:rgba(134,169,143,0.14); --accent-edge:rgba(134,169,143,0.35);
      --bad:#c98a7d; --bad-wash:rgba(201,138,125,0.12);
      /* The bridge logo is white on the dark page (owner, 25 Oct) and dark on the light one, where white would not show. */
      --logo:#ffffff;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing:border-box; }
  body { margin:0; background:var(--ground); color:var(--ink-body); font:16px/1.6 var(--sans); }
  .wrap { max-width:960px; margin:0 auto; padding:48px 24px 64px; }
  a { color:var(--accent); text-decoration:none; border-bottom:1px solid var(--accent-edge); }
  a:hover { color:var(--accent-hi); border-color:var(--accent-hi); }
  a.ext::after { content:" ↗"; font-size:.8em; color:var(--ink-dim); }
  header { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:14px; margin-bottom:8px; }
  header svg { width:34px; height:34px; color:var(--logo); }
  h1 { margin:0; font-size:2rem; color:var(--ink); letter-spacing:-.01em; }
  .tag { font:500 .75rem var(--mono); color:var(--accent); background:var(--accent-wash); border:1px solid var(--accent-edge); border-radius:999px; padding:2px 10px; }
  .lead { font-size:1.15rem; color:var(--ink-muted); margin:6px 0 36px; max-width:46em; }
  h2 { font-size:.8rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.12em; color:var(--ink-dim); margin:44px 0 14px; padding-bottom:8px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); }
  .grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr)); gap:16px; }
  .card { background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--edge); border-radius:10px; padding:20px; min-width:0; }
  .card h3 { margin:0 0 4px; color:var(--ink); font-size:1.1rem; }
  .card p { margin:0 0 14px; color:var(--ink-muted); font-size:.95rem; }
  .btn { display:inline-block; font-weight:600; color:var(--ground); background:var(--accent); border:0; border-radius:6px; padding:8px 14px; }
  .btn:hover { color:var(--ground); background:var(--accent-hi); }
  .creds { margin-top:14px; font:14px/1.9 var(--mono); color:var(--ink-code); }
  .creds b { display:inline-block; width:90px; color:var(--ink-dim); font-weight:400; }
  .creds code { background:var(--ground); border:1px solid var(--edge); border-radius:4px; padding:1px 8px; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-all; }
  .copy { font:12px var(--sans); color:var(--accent); background:none; border:1px solid var(--accent-edge); border-radius:4px; padding:1px 8px; margin-left:6px; cursor:pointer; }
  ol.steps { padding-left:1.3em; } ol.steps li { margin:6px 0; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x:auto; }
  table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:.95rem; }
  th { text-align:left; font-weight:500; color:var(--ink-dim); font-size:.8rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--edge); }
  td { padding:12px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align:top; }
  td.n { font-family:var(--mono); color:var(--ink-dim); }
  .v { font:600 .78rem var(--mono); border-radius:4px; padding:2px 8px; white-space:nowrap; }
  .v.ok { color:var(--accent); background:var(--accent-wash); }
  .v.bad { color:var(--bad); background:var(--bad-wash); }
  a.btn-sm { font:600 .78rem var(--mono); color:var(--accent); background:var(--accent-wash); border:1px solid var(--accent-edge); border-radius:4px; padding:2px 10px; white-space:nowrap; }
  a.btn-sm:hover { color:var(--accent-hi); border-color:var(--accent-hi); }
  .muted { color:var(--ink-muted); font-size:.9rem; }
  .scn .card { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:2px; }
  .scn .card p b { color:var(--ink); }
  .scn .card .btn, .scn .card a.ext { align-self:flex-start; margin-top:auto; }
  .scn .card a.ext { margin-top:10px; }
  .scn .card .creds { margin-top:auto; }
  footer { margin-top:56px; padding-top:16px; border-top:1px solid var(--rule); color:var(--ink-dim); font-size:.85rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1.5 18h21"/><path d="M6.4 18L7.5 7 8.6 18"/><path d="M7.5 7V3"/><path d="M7.5 5.5l6 12.5M7.5 7.5l10 10.5M7.5 9.5l13 8.5"/><path d="M7.5 6L2.5 18"/><circle cx="16" cy="18" r="1.8" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg>
  <h1>Your Proven lab is ready</h1>
  <span class="tag">running on your machine</span>
</header>
<p class="lead">Proven is a code reviewer that only reports a problem it can prove. This lab is a small Git server with a
demo repository, a CI runner that calls Proven on every pull request, and a dashboard that shows each review as it happens.
Nothing here leaves your machine unless you went live.</p>
<p class="muted" id="mode">Mode: <b>@@LAB_MODE@@</b>.</p>
<p class="muted" id="features">Meterless features, as this lab passed them to the review: <b>@@LAB_FEATURES@@</b>.</p>

<h2>Open</h2>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Pull requests</h3>
    <p>The demo repository in Gitea. Every pull request carries Proven's review as a comment.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="@@GITEA_URL@@/@@LAB_ADMIN_USER@@/@@LAB_DEMO_REPO@@/pulls?state=all" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Gitea</a>
    <div class="creds">
      <div><b>Username</b><code id="u">@@LAB_ADMIN_USER@@</code><button class="copy" data-copy="u">copy</button></div>
      <div><b>Password</b><code id="p">@@LAB_PASSWORD@@</code><button class="copy" data-copy="p">copy</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Dashboards</h3>
    <p>Grafana, six dashboards: every pull request at a glance, one review in detail, the evidence, the models and the guardrail, the Meterless engines, Nightshift.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="@@GRAFANA_URL@@" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Grafana</a>
    <div class="creds">
      <div><a href="@@GRAFANA_BASE@@/d/proven-review" target="_blank" rel="noopener">One review</a> &middot; <a href="@@GRAFANA_BASE@@/d/proven-evidence" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Evidence</a> &middot; <a href="@@GRAFANA_BASE@@/d/proven-models" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Models and trust</a></div>
      <div><a href="@@GRAFANA_BASE@@/d/proven-engines" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Meterless engines</a> &middot; <a href="@@GRAFANA_BASE@@/d/proven-nightshift" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nightshift</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Documentation</h3>
    <p>How Proven works, every setting, the decisions behind it. Served from this lab, works offline.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="@@DOCS_URL@@" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the docs</a>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Help</h3>
    <p>The step-by-step walkthrough, and <code>docs/LAB.md</code> for troubleshooting.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="@@HELP_URL@@" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the walkthrough</a>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>What Proven does: try it yourself</h2>
<p class="muted">Six things, each in plain words: what happens, what you see, and a button that runs it here. The first three are the demo pull requests already in this lab.</p>
<div class="grid scn">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>A clean change passes</h3>
    <p><b>What happens.</b> Proven reads a small, correct change, runs the tests on the base and on the change, and checks its dependencies.</p>
    <p><b>What you see.</b> A short "clean" verdict that says what was checked. No false alarm.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="@@PAGE_URL@@/report/@@PR_discount-clean@@.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try yourself: open the review</a>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>A vulnerable dependency is blocked</h3>
    <p><b>What happens.</b> A change adds a library whose version is inside a known-vulnerable range. Proven asks Zetaris, which holds the OSV, KEV and EPSS advisory tables.</p>
    <p><b>What you see.</b> "Blocked", with the advisory rows that matched, each under its query.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="@@PAGE_URL@@/report/@@PR_osv-go-module@@.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try yourself: open the review</a>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>A code defect is blocked by a failing test</h3>
    <p><b>What happens.</b> A change takes a discount off twice. Proven writes a test, runs it on the base and on the change, and keeps the finding only because the test fails on the change and passes on the base.</p>
    <p><b>What you see.</b> "Blocked", with the failing test and its output.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="@@PAGE_URL@@/report/@@PR_discount@@.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try yourself: open the review</a>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>A forged evidence pack is refused</h3>
    <p><b>What happens.</b> Every review can leave one signed evidence pack. One byte of a copy is changed after it was signed.</p>
    <p><b>What you see.</b> <code>proven verify</code> accepts the real pack and refuses the changed copy, naming the check that failed.</p>
    <div class="creds"><div><code id="c-forged">make try SCENARIO=forged</code><button class="copy" data-copy="c-forged">copy</button></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>The Prover has no network and no secret</h3>
    <p><b>What happens.</b> The Prover runs a test in a container with no network, no password or token passed in, and the code mounted read-only.</p>
    <p><b>What you see.</b> A container with those flags tries to reach the network, find a secret and change the code, and fails at all three.</p>
    <div class="creds"><div><code id="c-prover">make try SCENARIO=prover</code><button class="copy" data-copy="c-prover">copy</button></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>The Meterless engines, on and off</h3>
    <p><b>What happens.</b> H-MEM, Scout Intent, Markovian and the World Model help a review. Two of them can be switched off for a run: <code>make up PROVEN_MARKOVIAN=off PROVEN_LAB_SCOUT_INTENT=off</code>.</p>
    <p><b>What you see.</b> The same reviews, and on the Engines dashboard what each engine did.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="@@GRAFANA_BASE@@/d/proven-engines" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try yourself: open the engines</a>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Security: code and image</h2>
<p class="muted">Two reviews, side by side. Each claim links to the live proof, not to a picture of it.</p>
<div class="grid scn">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Code review</h3>
    <p>Proven reports a problem only with its evidence: a query on advisory data, or a test that fails on the change and passes before it. A claim it cannot prove, or that its own Skeptic refutes, is dropped.</p>
    <p><b>Live proof.</b> The review of each demo pull request is a comment in Gitea in this lab, and the same reviews run on every change to Proven's own repository.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="@@GITEA_URL@@/@@LAB_ADMIN_USER@@/@@LAB_DEMO_REPO@@/pulls?state=all" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The comments in this lab</a>
    <a class="ext" href="https://github.com/saphan-ai/proven/actions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The build pipeline on GitHub Actions</a>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Image security review</h3>
    <p>The image this lab runs is scanned by Docker Scout on every build, with its software bill of materials and its build provenance attached to the image.</p>
    <p><b>Live proof.</b> The image on Docker Hub, with Docker Scout's own result for it.</p>
    <a class="btn ext" href="https://hub.docker.com/r/saphan/proven" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The image on Docker Hub</a>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Is every review done?</h2>
<p class="muted">Reviews take a few minutes each. <code>make up</code> waits for all of them before it says the lab is ready, so the dashboards already have data. To wait again, or to check a lab you started earlier, run <code>make demo-check</code>. Outside the repository's folder: <code>make -C &lt;path to the repository&gt; demo-check</code>. It prints one line per pull request, and how many reviews reached the dashboards.</p>

<h2>The scenario</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li>Open Gitea and sign in with the user and password above.</li>
  <li>Open the pull requests. @@CLEAN_COUNT@@ are clean changes; the others each carry a different kind of defect.</li>
  <li>Read Proven's comment on each one. A clean change gets a short "clean" verdict that says what was checked.
      A defect is reported only with its evidence: the query that found it, or a test that fails on the change and passes before it.</li>
  <li>Open the dashboard and pick a review. You see each agent's step and both reviewers' verdicts for the same change.</li>
  <li>Reviews take a few minutes each. A pull request with no comment yet is still being reviewed.</li>
</ol>

